TEXT -912 -384 Left 4 ;#232 Transistor curve tracer using stairstep base drive
TEXT -912 -304 Left 3 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZOLLoa2fH24
TEXT -912 -248 Left 3 ;A stepped base current and repeating collector-voltage sweep reveal a family of NPN collector curves.
TEXT -912 1152 Left 2 !.ic V(OUT)=0 V(CLOCK)=0
TEXT -912 1184 Left 2 !.tran 0 16.6m 11.2m 1u
TEXT -912 1216 Left 2 !.option plotwinsize=0
TEXT -200 1152 Left 2 !.meas tran STEP_V MAX V(OUT) FROM 11.5m TO 16.5m
TEXT -200 1184 Left 2 !.meas tran VX_MAX MAX V(X) FROM 11.5m TO 16.5m
TEXT -200 1216 Left 2 !.meas tran VY_MAX MAX V(Y) FROM 11.5m TO 16.5m
TEXT -200 1248 Left 2 !.meas tran IC_MAX PARAM VY_MAX/270
TEXT 560 1152 Left 2 !.meas tran IB_MAX PARAM STEP_V/470k
TEXT -912 1312 Left 2 !.include "..\..\LTspice\Models\National Semiconductor\LMC6482A.lib"
TEXT -912 1368 Left 2 ;X is the device-under-test collector voltage and Y is the mirrored collector current across the 270 ohm sense resistor.\nAlan's drawing names the transistor types but not part numbers, so the 2N3904 and 2N3906 models are simulation choices.
